^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-20 14:56] observe — mount documentation is mostly substrate-oriented, but active plans still name individual consumers and editor comparison claims no longer match the LSP-backed implementation.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:57] decide — use `consumer repository`, `consumer-owned .spw`, and `mounted workbench` as the portable vocabulary; identifiers and local locations are never fixture requirements.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:58] decide — audit editor surfaces by author task, protocol capability, observed evidence, failure behavior, and ownership layer rather than feature parity.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:59] taste — CLI observability is the prerequisite: root discovery, mount health, capabilities, and machine-readable evidence should make editor audits reproducible instead of anecdotal.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:00] revise — remove specific domains from active code and canon, not only mounted-review examples; preserve reusable qualities as identity-free surface archetypes whose future deployment remains unspecified.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:32] implement — retired identifier-aware init behavior and the named registry; added portable archetypes, mount authority rules, editor evidence axes, and a mounted-consumer review skill.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:33] revise — LSP and editor plans now begin with advertised/configured/invoked/observed/tested audits; custom requests and cross-editor presentation are conditional on demonstrated author tasks.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:31] transfer — mounted-workbench-organelle turns the authority protocol into an executable orientation ladder: prompt, roots, bounded tree, selectors, and editor landmarks.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:20] verify — portability vocabulary, surface archetypes, mounted-consumer review procedure, authority exclusions, and identity-free fixtures are landed foundations; future changes are protocol maintenance, not continuation of the original seven-commit feature plan.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:24] decide — consumer exchange reports exclude the mount, use relative/redacted paths, carry consumer and workbench revisions, and return capability gaps or workload shapes rather than copying domain canon upstream.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:25] decide — establish a zero-annotation floor: ordinary package and source structure must yield useful inventory, navigation, performance, and migration evidence before any Spw feature tags are adopted.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:26] taste — optional annotations earn adoption through concrete recognizability, impact, and projection benefits; they remain removable and never certify authorship, belonging, or project understanding.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:36] observe — an identity-free consumer uses its sidecar as a fluid semantic topography that points back to crystallized code and proof surfaces; the sidecar explicitly says it summons rather than documents the system.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:37] decide — consumer exchange records sidecar posture, source revision/back-reference, and promotion state so interpretive lenses can remain useful without being mistaken for implementation truth.
 >>[2026-08-24 13:05] observe — a read-only two-revision corpus probe found positional-file versus --from inconsistency, lossy JSON snippets, no stdin/range/profile source inspection, success without intended-root completeness, mount-note revision drift, and insufficient exclusion disclosure.
 >>[2026-08-24 13:06] decide — promote these as identity-free protocol gaps: machine products separate exact data from bounded display, parser receipts state consumption/root expectations, and doctor compares declared versus observed mount revisions.
 >>[2026-08-24 13:07] decide — cross-project state projections declare channel geometry, normalization, ordering, and loss; thresholded expressions, color, and cultural labels cannot stand in for recoverable state or automatically confer genre.
}

